{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/528243-convince-a-player-to-try-scion-when-they-just-say-why-not-exalted","id":528243,"title":"convince a player to try scion when they just say why not exalted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-25T17:00:09-07:00","id":528243,"title":"convince a player to try scion when they just say why not exalted","content":"one of my players looks at scion and just sees exalted how do i change that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5414-druzil94","name":"Druzil94","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T17:10:08-07:00","id":528254,"title":"","content":"It's the difference between Dragon Ball Z and Hercules: the Legendary Journey. The themes are very similar, the power scale is similar, the powers... are better written in Exalted, actually. The mechanics, too. And the setting makes more sense. If your player isn't into mythology, they're not going to be into Scion. It's a different genre. Exalted is Anime, Scion is Myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T21:17:04-07:00","id":528486,"title":"","content":"Scion Pro: Actual Mythology. Great concept.<br /> Scion Con: Rules are a mess.<br /> <br /> Exalted Pro: Heck of a lot of things, actually.<br /> Exalted Con: Rules are ridiculously crunchy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T00:07:09-07:00","id":529653,"title":"","content":"I'm so sorry. Every post I make just turns into one that's trying to convince you to ditch Scion for Exalted. The best I can do is offer a compare and contrast.<br /> <br /> If you want to play in a world where the world is flat, The Gods are crackheads that left you the keys to the world and the people currently running it are out to get you, you play Exalted.<br /> <br /> If you want to play in a world where it's <i>your world</i>. The one you live, during any given era, but all the myths and gods and monsters and other crazy things that people believed before toliet paper are <i>real</i>, you play Scion.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T00:17:05-07:00","id":529658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Druzil94</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/528243-convince-a-player-to-try-scion-when-they-just-say-why-not-exalted#post528243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one of my players looks at scion and just sees exalted how do i change that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The quesion here is more what do they want to play? (and if I remember correctly scion 1st ed rules were based on exalted rules so seeing one in the other is quite possible there).<br /> <br /> I myself did not really read much into exalted back then but from what I remember the summaries so far catch most of the difference:<br /> Exalted is more or less like an anime. And if you go by the core setting its set in a fantasy world that is vastly different form our own.<br /> Scion on the other hand is pure mythology. And if you go by the core setting it is set in the modern world which is quite like our own only that mythology runs rampant. <br /> <br /> Thus if you want to play an anime its exalted, if you like mythology on the other hand (or want to play percy jackson) scion catches that feeling a bit better than exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T00:26:15-07:00","id":529666,"title":"","content":"Honestly setting is probably going to be your best bet. I mean the two share enough similarities from what I've seen that I figure you'd be aiming more for which has the most hits on interest as opposed to liking one or the other. Back to my point Scion assumes modern world meaning you can totally play an inventor type who's decked out his car to fight a war if someone gets passed your best friend the sniper war god. As another bonus Scion has a few more incentives preventing the permakill of major threats. Like it comes up every once in a while in the Exalted forum on how to slay a Yozi and smack around Deathlords and why has nobody just done this crap already. As I understand it permanently killing a titan in Scion has a mention of abruptly ending an ice age with the indication that killing these things is probably not going to help the problem. As a result you could probably make a case that it requires a bit more thought to deal with than the utter annoying BS of &quot;I stab the endless desert repeatedly and then use ghost eating technique so it dies forever and ever and I'm clever,&quot; that crops up in Exalted from time to time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T23:06:10-07:00","id":530712,"title":"","content":"The biggest appeals of Scion to me is that it is a modern fantasy setting which is my favorite genre, and that the setting is much more open to being customized to fit the story you are trying to tell. One of the pitfalls of Exalted having such a developed setting is that is is easy to get hung up on that setting and what is &quot;canon&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T15:11:01-07:00","id":534881,"title":"","content":"Tell them that we'll get Scion 2e before we get Exalted 3e? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But seriously: the appeal of Scion lies in it being a mythology-based modern fantasy setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T21:01:41-07:00","id":539162,"title":"","content":"The games can run the same way; they're both massively powerful characters empowered by gods, etc.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the feel of the two is radically different.<br /> <br /> Scion is informed by ancient myth, but layers it into the real world. This results in a feel like American Gods, or like Matt Wagner's Mage comics. This is important and relevant to differentiating the two because the feel of the game is specifically about combining particular things that are specifically familiar to the audience. We have centaurs, for instance, but they're also a biker gang. The specific mix of human legend and the familiar mundane is critical to the game--and in my experience hard to nail perfectly--especially at the Hero level, but even at the highest points of Godhood you're walking with things relevant to history that you could probably look up on the web or your local library, and you have roots in the world we live in here and now. <br /> <br /> Exalted on the other hand...well, it's an odd duck. Also a very cool duck. What is familiar is in aesthetics, and individual bits of setting, but they're sliced and diced and meshed in ways that are separated from any historical context. See, for instance, how the Realm is a mishmash of Rome and Persia and Imperial China, for instance. Also, while the Exalted have a strong sense of the Legendary about them, they also have something else: Reading the pulp fantasy that fed into the suggested reading of 1e made a lot of things click into focus, but there's also very much the anime-inspired action-driven aesthetic. Creation has its own mythology, and it's one that can be fascinating and often draws on familiar archetypes, but it is not the world we know in any real way.<br /> <br /> They have some very strong similarities, but they're also significantly different and at least intended to tell different stories.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}